Subject: Post FSC5 Implementation Readiness Surface V1
Date: 2026-05-26
Surface UUID: 0608e6ff-ecb3-4ded-86a5-3b8d59670410

@ [canonical_specification] docs/canonical/LangSOP_Post_FSC5_Implementation_Readiness.canonical.sop
@ [source_manifest] docs/source/2026-05-26_post_fsc5_implementation_readiness/Source_Document_Manifest.sop
@ [foundation_pack] docs/planning/FSC1_Foundation_Contract_Pack.v1.sop
@ [planning_coordination_pack] docs/planning/FSC2_Planning_Coordination_Pack.v1.sop
@ [runtime_graph_pack] docs/planning/FSC3_Runtime_Graph_Proof_Pack.v1.sop
@ [surface_projection_pack] docs/planning/FSC4_Surface_Projection_Pack.v1.sop
@ [operations_safety_pack] docs/planning/FSC5_Operations_Safety_Pack.v1.sop

& [PostFSC5ImplementationReadinessSurfaceV1] is the current implementation-readiness surface after FSC1 through FSC5 acceptance
  + [surface_state] is ready_for_IR1_slice_minting
  + [accepted_boundary_input] is FSC1FoundationContractPackV1
  + [accepted_boundary_input] is FSC2PlanningCoordinationPackV1
  + [accepted_boundary_input] is FSC3RuntimeGraphProofPackV1
  + [accepted_boundary_input] is FSC4SurfaceProjectionPackV1
  + [accepted_boundary_input] is FSC5OperationsSafetyPackV1
  + [active_implementation_chunk] is IR1 implementation substrate and repository scaffold
  + [gated_chunk] is IR2 until IR1 accepted
  + [gated_chunk] is IR3 until IR2 accepted
  + [gated_chunk] is IR4 until IR3 accepted
  + [gated_chunk] is IR5 until IR4 accepted
  + [gated_chunk] is IR6 until IR5 accepted
  + [gated_chunk] is IR7 until IR6 accepted and operations safety remains accepted
  + [safety_limit] is no live operations control authorized

  = must: mint IR1 final slices before writing runtime code
  = must: run completion review after each implementation slice before opening downstream chunks
  = must: preserve SOP source files as authority and generated indexes as projections
  = must: keep operations dry-run-only unless a separate future live-control authority is source-preserved, SJS-processed, and accepted

& [ImplementationReadinessChunk: IR1ImplementationSubstrateAndRepositoryScaffold] is ready_for_slice_minting
  + [chunk_id] is IR1
  + [chunk_name] is implementation substrate and repository scaffold
  + [boundary_input_set] is docs/planning/FSC1_Foundation_Contract_Pack.v1.sop
  + [boundary_input_set] is docs/planning/FSC2_Planning_Coordination_Pack.v1.sop
  + [boundary_input_set] is docs/planning/FSC5_Operations_Safety_Pack.v1.sop
  + [expected_output_set] is implementation language and package decision, repo layout contract, generated artifact policy, test harness shape, and scaffold final slices
  + [model_route] is requires deeper reasoning
  + [model_route_reason] is repository shape and generated projection boundaries affect authority, storage, tests, and downstream implementation safety
  + [forbidden_scope] is parser implementation, SQLite builder implementation, LangGraph runtime implementation, UI implementation, adapter implementation, operations simulator implementation, live operations control, and live machine control

  = must: split IR1 into final slices before code scaffolding

& [ImplementationReadinessChunk: IR2AuthorityParserAndSQLiteProjectionBuilder] is gated
  + [chunk_id] is IR2
  + [chunk_name] is authority-file parser and SQLite projection builder
  + [activation_gate] is IR1 accepted
  + [expected_output_set] is parser contract implementation, authority record extraction, hash ledger validation, SQLite projection builder, and parser/projection fixtures
  + [model_route] is requires deeper reasoning for parser and projection authority boundary; GPT-5.3-Codex-Spark-suitable for bounded fixtures after contracts are accepted
  + [forbidden_scope] is treating SQLite as authority or silently modifying SOP sources

& [ImplementationReadinessChunk: IR3OperatorHarnessAndFixtureRunner] is gated
  + [chunk_id] is IR3
  + [chunk_name] is operator harness and fixture runner
  + [activation_gate] is IR2 accepted
  + [expected_output_set] is contract-driven operator runner, fixture runner, trace output writer, and foundation/planning fixture execution
  + [model_route] is GPT-5.3-Codex-Spark-suitable after IR1 and IR2 accepted
  + [forbidden_scope] is dispatch, live operations, hidden authority writes, and unreviewed runtime graph integration

& [ImplementationReadinessChunk: IR4LangGraphProofRuntimeImplementation] is gated
  + [chunk_id] is IR4
  + [chunk_name] is LangGraph proof runtime implementation
  + [activation_gate] is IR3 accepted
  + [expected_output_set] is minimal WholeFieldPlannerGraph implementation, checkpoint policy implementation, SOP-first interrupt path, and runtime graph fixtures
  + [model_route] is requires deeper reasoning for graph integration and interrupt semantics; GPT-5.3-Codex-Spark-suitable for bounded graph fixtures after proof contracts are accepted
  + [forbidden_scope] is checkpoint authority promotion, hidden graph writes, surface authority promotion, and operations control

& [ImplementationReadinessChunk: IR5SurfaceProjectionPrototype] is gated
  + [chunk_id] is IR5
  + [chunk_name] is surface projection prototype
  + [activation_gate] is IR4 accepted
  + [expected_output_set] is manager, worker, narrative, debug, conversation, adapter, and optional Langflow projection prototypes over fixture records
  + [model_route] is GPT-5.3-Codex-Spark-suitable for bounded projection prototype after fixture records exist, with deeper reasoning for authority display conflicts
  + [forbidden_scope] is treating surface, adapter, chat, terminal, IRC, Matrix, web, Langflow, or Codex state as source authority

& [ImplementationReadinessChunk: IR6CoordinationMailboxAndClaimProjectionPrototype] is gated
  + [chunk_id] is IR6
  + [chunk_name] is coordination mailbox and claim projection prototype
  + [activation_gate] is IR5 accepted
  + [expected_output_set] is coordination claim projection, rendezvous packet projection, mailbox projection, conflict signal fixtures, and multi-agent work boundary proof
  + [model_route] is requires deeper reasoning for identity, conflict, and multi-agent coordination semantics
  + [forbidden_scope] is dispatching agents, collapsing conversation identities, or treating mailbox carriers as signed authority

& [ImplementationReadinessChunk: IR7OperationsDryRunRequestSimulator] is gated
  + [chunk_id] is IR7
  + [chunk_name] is operations dry-run request simulator
  + [activation_gate] is IR6 accepted
  + [activation_gate] is FSC5OperationsSafetyPackV1 remains accepted
  + [expected_output_set] is dry-run-only operation request simulator, refusal output records, safety fixture execution, and no-live-effect proof
  + [model_route] is requires deeper reasoning for operations dry-run simulator boundaries
  + [forbidden_scope] is command execution, process control, GPU control, model runtime mutation, job dispatch, credential access or mutation, network exposure mutation, destructive filesystem action, persistent operations automation, and live machine control

  = must: preserve dry-run-only semantics and refuse live effects as records

& [PostFSC5ReadinessClosureReview] is the dependency audit for the post-FSC5 implementation surface
  + [FSC1_pack_status] is accepted
  + [FSC2_pack_status] is accepted
  + [FSC3_pack_status] is accepted
  + [FSC4_pack_status] is accepted
  + [FSC5_pack_status] is accepted
  + [current_ready_chunk_set] is IR1
  + [unresolved_external_dependency_set] is empty_after_gate
  + [forbidden_external_dependency_found] is false
  + [operations_control_authorized] is false
  + [live_machine_control_authorized] is false

  = must: treat IR2 through IR7 as gated, not ready
  = must: rerun closure review when a boundary pack changes, proof fails, or implementation contradiction appears
